capability quat/identity  the quaternion of no rotation
  heroes  linear.identity_quat
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  odin    QUATERNIONF64_IDENTITY, quaternion_from_scalar

capability quat/axis-angle  a quaternion from an axis and an angle, and back
  heroes  linear.rotation_quat, linear.to_axis_angle, linear.AxisAngle
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  odin    quaternion_angle_axis, angle_axis_from_quaternion, axis_from_quaternion, angle_from_quaternion
  note    the angle answered from 0 to pi, the quaternion turned to a non-negative real part first

capability quat/euler  a rotation from three angles about the axes of a named order, and back
  heroes  linear.euler_quat, linear.to_euler, linear.axes_of, linear.Euler, linear.EulerOrder
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  odin    Euler_Angle_Order, quaternion_from_euler_angles, quaternion_from_euler_angle_x, quaternion_from_euler_angle_y, quaternion_from_euler_angle_z, euler_angles_from_quaternion, euler_angles_xyz_from_quaternion, euler_angles_xzy_from_quaternion, euler_angles_yxz_from_quaternion, euler_angles_yzx_from_quaternion, euler_angles_zxy_from_quaternion, euler_angles_zyx_from_quaternion, euler_angles_xyx_from_quaternion, euler_angles_xzx_from_quaternion, euler_angles_yxy_from_quaternion, euler_angles_yzy_from_quaternion, euler_angles_zxz_from_quaternion, euler_angles_zyz_from_quaternion, euler_angles_from_matrixN, the twelve euler_angles_..._from_matrixN, matrixN_from_euler_angles, the twelve matrixN_from_euler_angles_..., matrixN_from_euler_angles_xy, _xz, _yx, _yz, _zx, _zy, quaternion_from_pitch_yaw_roll, pitch_yaw_roll_from_quaternion, pitch_from_quaternion, yaw_from_quaternion, roll_from_quaternion, matrixN_from_yaw_pitch_roll
  note    the twelve orders, Tait and Bryan's six and Euler's six proper ones, every turn about the axes as the turns before left them; a matrix from angles is `linear.to_mat3` of the quaternion, two angles a third of 0, and yaw, pitch and roll an order (`zyx` for a frame whose z is up). Taken back with no threshold for gimbal lock: the third angle from the matrix with the first turn taken out, so the angles rebuild the rotation to its last bits in every order (run 2026-11-17)

